> and the outside world.  However, since I don't see any sort of prompt
> at all, that's probably not the problem now.

Why don't you first verify which of the two works and then try to
hook them up to each other?

The DS10 should automatically default to serial console, even if
"graphics" is set in SRM.  It's the first port and by default
indeed with that setup.

I assume the 'extra layer' you're referring to is RMC.  That's
not invoked by default, one must call it via: Esc Esc R M C
(thus, in other words: tapping Escape twice, or Ctrl/[, and after
that sequentially typing: "R", "M", "C" .)

  - MG



